	quests: [
		{
			title: "FOP Digitalization"
			icon: "tfb2:fop_digitalizer"
			x: -3.5d
			y: -1.25d
			shape: "diamond"
			description: [
				"&7Other than running Vaults, the FOP pay you for 'Digitalizing' items with their Digitalizer."
				""
				"&7Which really is just a fancy tool that teleports the items to them and gives you back 'tokens', which you can collect and....boom, turn them into Vault Coins! Another form of token, of course. This one just represents the standard FOP Game Server Currency."
				""
				"&7They don't accept cheap things like Dirt or Cobblestone. Why should they, technically they already have it in their system. And they pay a tenth of a haypenny for slightly bigger things, like String and Feathers."
				""
				"&7Instead they tempt you with PROCESSING those cheap resources into bigger things, and paying you slightly more for those. One Redstone Dust only gets you a couple bits back, but take the time to craft it with some Wood and make a Note Block? Well, now its worth (very slightly) more!"
			]
			dependencies: ["668288F6DA34369B"]
			id: "03A5DD093C9AB5D6"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "2E24DB252CBB9771"
					type: "item"
					item: "tfb2:fop_digitalizer"
				}
				{
					id: "29312C03D0A7D58E"
					type: "item"
					item: "tfb2:fop_digitalized_item"
					count: 50L
				}
			]
			rewards: [{
				id: "56418F0868B7EEAF"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			x: -0.25d
			y: -1.25d
			shape: "diamond"
			description: [
				"&7So, the primary way you get money from The Ferret Business is by following our various Research questlines. For following instructions and helping us test products at the same time (and find new ways to infect the FOP game server), you get paid in Ferret Dollars and Blind Boxes."
				""
				"&7But, you aren't going to use all the items you make during research. And you'll find and gather a lot of other items along the way, yeah? So the other way you get Ferret Dollars is by shipping them to us at home with the Shipping System."
				""
				"&7We keep about half the items you send us for our own stockpiles. The other half gets put back into the FOP Game Server, helping to spread the Audubon Worm. Two birds, one stone, yeah?"
				""
				"&7As much as we'd like to accept everything, the FOP Game Server doesn't bother 'buying' or even tracking cheap stuff. Anything about 24 FMC worth or below is not tracked, so we won't waste computing power with it for now."
			]
			dependencies: ["668288F6DA34369B"]
			id: "086FFB8B8B787C40"
			tasks: [{
				id: "214EA83BE9F4F7C9"
				type: "item"
				item: "projecte:transmutation_table"
			}]
			rewards: [{
				id: "37DD6884060575A2"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "TFB Trade Order System"
			icon: "wares:sealed_delivery_agreement"
			x: -2.0d
			y: 1.25d
			shape: "diamond"
			description: [
				"&7There's a lot of Power Users trapped in the system, Bandit, and most of them don't have the strength to do much more than survive."
				""
				"&7Bandit, you're in a unique position : with the Business behind you, and a mission to break the system, we can help out both regular Users and Power Users."
				""
				"&7We're bringing in our old Contracts system, but changing it up. They'll be called Trade Orders now."
				""
				"&7We'll need to implement them in a way that won't trip the FOP Security Systems immediately..."
				""
				"&7Let's see....Okay I got it."
				""
				"&7We'll call this...Wares. Like shop wares. You'll need to find a Sealed Trade Order by looting them in Flesh Chests in Raw Vaults or Coin Piles in normal Vaults."
				""
				"&7We can also offer a couple Sealed Trade Orders in the Shop Tablet, but only every 5 days for safety."
				""
			]
			dependencies: ["668288F6DA34369B"]
			id: "288B4CFEEC379A41"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7E85E665FFC1AC27"
				type: "item"
				item: "tfb2:trade_order_cheap"
			}]
			rewards: [
				{
					id: "4E8EF7BEF3C478AD"
					type: "choice"
					table_id: 2640422954496342337L
				}
				{
					id: "74624EFC794D79FC"
					type: "item"
					item: "tfb2:trade_order_cheap"
				}
			]
		}
		{
			title: "What're Ya Trading?"
			icon: "wares:delivery_agreement"
			x: -2.0d
			y: 2.5d
			shape: "rsquare"
			description: [
				"&7When you obtain a Sealed Trade Contract, it will be one of four tiers, much like our Blind Boxes : Cheap, Decent, Good, and Amazing."
				""
				"&7Hold and Right Click the Sealed Contract to unseal it. You'll get a Trade Order with the Username and Server it came from, along with a short message, and most importantly : What they want, and what they are offering. There will also be a number for how many times you can fill this Trade Order."
				""
				"&7The value of the items depends on the tier, and you'll usually be rewarded roughly 50% more FMC value for filling the Trade Order."
				""
				"&7Downside? The items requested may be from a mod you haven't Researched yet..."
				""
				"&7Upside? The items you are being PAID with may also be from a mod you haven't researched yet!"
			]
			dependencies: ["288B4CFEEC379A41"]
			id: "047154F810F692A4"
			tasks: [{
				id: "3CD79966C92048F4"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Shipping Packages"
			icon: "wares:delivery_table"
			x: -2.0d
			y: 3.75d
			shape: "rsquare"
			description: [
				"&7When you have a Trade Order you want to fill, and the items to fill it with, you'll need a [TFB] Delivery Table. And some [TFB] Cardboard Boxes as well."
				""
				"&7Set down the Delivery Table, and toss some of those boxes into the bottom center. The Trade Order goes in the top center. When you add the items to the left, the Arrow in the center will highlight as a button. Click it to start shipping items manually."
				""
				"&7Shipping items manually will take about 3 minutes per order."
				""
				"&7If you want to ship faster, you'll have to hire a Packager Villager. It works like any other Villager profession: the Delivery Table is their job block."
				""
				"&7With a Packager, orders will ship 3 times faster while they are working. But Villagers don't work 24/7, and until the Packager levels up (by successfully shipping out items), they'll be somewhat slow."
			]
			dependencies: ["047154F810F692A4"]
			id: "62D5F301E541E3FA"
